inking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe established workflow prioritizes thorough investigation, planning, and explicit approval before any code modifications, ensuring adherence to project constraints. Code modifications must be devoid of in-code documentation and adhere strictly to the approved architecture and implementation plan, preventing improvisation or scope creep. The restrictions on in-code documentation and code improvements apply across the entire implementation.\n\n\nThe project avoids external dependencies by utilizing standard browser ES Modules from a CDN and requires no build tools for Vercel deployment, optimizing for immediate static edge performance. Performance optimizations include the Fisher-Yates shuffle algorithm for randomization, reusable DOM updates, debouncing for minimal database writes, and single document reads to minimize Firestore operations. The implementation requires adherence to zero in-code documentation.\n\n\nFirebase read operations are optimized by reading quiz data once per student session, adhering to Firestore free tier limits and minimizing database interactions. CSS styles and Firebase configuration leverage modular design principles and shared components to avoid redundancy. Security rules will be updated in Firebase Console to permit read/write operations for the quiz and teacher editor without authentication, documented in an `implementation_plan.md` artifact.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan for creating a Firebase-backed quiz system (Student Quiz site + Teacher Quiz Creator & Editor site) based strictly on QUIZ06 design, ready for Vercel deployment.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan: Firebase-Backed Quiz System for Vercel\n\n## 1. System Overview & Architecture\n\nWe will implement two web interfaces designed specifically for static deployment to Vercel, integrating with Google Cloud Firestore using the provided Firebase project credentials (`sir-jasper-quiz`):\n\n1. **Student Quiz Application (`index.html`)**:\n   - Fetches active quiz questions, distractors, and teacher configuration from Firestore (`quizzes/active`).\n   - Retains exact styling, card aesthetics, CSS variables (light/dark mode), button states, alert overlays, and typography from `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`.\n   - Adopts teacher-configured features:\n     - Question randomization (toggleable via teacher config).\n     - Answer distractor randomization (toggleable via teacher config).\n     - Switching tab/window violation penalty and warnings (toggleable via teacher config).\n     - Countdown timer per question with progress bar (toggleable and configurable in seconds).\n   - Generates score results, downloadable JSON report, base64 result code string (`btoa(unescape(encodeURIComponent(...)))`), and per-question feedback matching the original structure.\n   - Local device lock prevents retaking the quiz unless reset via hash (`#reset-quiz`).\n\n2. **Teacher Quiz Creator & Editor Application (`teacher.html`)**:\n   - Strictly applies the visual design and component styles from `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`.\n   - Dynamic auto-numbered question list (\"Question 1\", \"Question 2\", etc.):\n     - Question input box (tap and type).\n     - Correct answer input box (tap and type).\n     - Wrong answer 1 input box (tap and type).\n     - Wrong answer 2 input box (tap and type).\n     - Wrong answer 3 input box (tap and type).\n     - Explanation input box (for per-question feedback).\n     - Delete question button for removing a question card.\n   - `+` Button: Appends a new question card below with auto-incremented numbering.\n   - `Options` Button: Opens an options configuration card/modal with toggles for:\n     - Auto randomize answers (ON/OFF).\n     - Auto randomize questions (ON/OFF).\n     - Switching tab violation penalty (ON/OFF and penalty points).\n     - Timer per question (ON/OFF and duration in seconds).\n   - Action controls:\n     - `Save & Publish to Firebase`: Writes questions and config to Firestore doc `quizzes/active`.\n     - `Load from Firebase`: Fetches the current published quiz.\n     - `Import Default C Quiz`: Preloads the 20 questions from the original HTML as a baseline template.\n     - Direct link button to open the student quiz (`index.html`).\n\n3. **Vercel Routing Configuration (`vercel.json`)**:\n   - Provides clean routing (`/` -> `index.html`, `/teacher` -> `teacher.html`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Affected Files\n\n| File | Action | Purpose |\n|------|--------|---------|\n| `index.html` | Create | Student quiz client connecting to Firestore and rendering quiz flow |\n| `teacher.html` | Create | Teacher question creator, editor, and option settings interface |\n| `vercel.json` | Create | Clean URL configuration for Vercel static deployment |\n| `HISTORY.md` | Create | Patch history tracking per Rule 1 |\n\n*(Note: `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` remains untouched as the reference template)*\n\n---\n\n## 3. Optimization & Performance Analysis\n\n1. **Zero-Build Static Architecture**:\n   - Pure ES modules via Google's official CDN (`https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.12.0/firebase-app.js` and `firebase-firestore.js`).\n   - Instant deployment on Vercel Edge CDN without compilation steps, dependencies, or build failures.\n2. **Firestore Free Tier Optimization (DRY & Cost Reduction)**:\n   - Consolidates quiz metadata, options, and question array into a single active document (`quizzes/active`).\n   - Every student quiz session uses exactly **1 Firestore read** (within the 50,000 daily free tier limit).\n   - Publishing from teacher interface uses exactly **1 Firestore write**.\n3. **Algorithm Efficiency**:\n   - Fisher-Yates shuffle algorithm ($O(n)$ time complexity, $O(1)$ auxiliary space) for unbiased question and answer randomization.\n   - Debounced state handling and DOM fragment updates to eliminate unnecessary reflows.\n4. **Constraint Enforcement (Rule 9)**:\n   - **Zero in-code documentation**: No code comments, docstrings, or TODO/FIXME markers in the generated codebase.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Risks & Mitigations\n\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|--------|------------|\n| Firestore Security Rules returning 403 `PERMISSION_DENIED` | Students or teacher cannot read/write questions | Provide the exact Firestore security rules snippet (`allow read, write: if true;`) for the Firebase console, and include clear UI status banners showing connection state. |\n| Network offline or Firebase temporarily unreachable | Student quiz blank or unresponsive | Fallback mechanism detects failure and provides an option to load cached/default questions or retry. |\n| Accidental overwrite of quiz by teacher | Data loss | Confirmation modal before publishing, and ability to load existing data first. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verification Plan\n\n### Automated & Local Verification:\n1. **File Syntax & Integrity Verification**:\n   - Validate HTML, CSS, and JS syntax across `index.html`, `teacher.html`, and `vercel.json`.\n   - Verify `HISTORY.md` has the new patch entry documented.\n2. **Local HTTP Server Emulation**:\n   - Serve the directory using Python or Node local HTTP server.\n   - Test `teacher.html`:\n     - Load default C questions.\n     - Add new question via `+` button and verify auto-numbering.\n     - Remove question and verify re-numbering.\n     - Open Options UI and toggle settings (randomize questions, randomize answers, violations, timer).\n     - Test Firestore write operation.\n   - Test `index.html`:\n     - Test fetching quiz from Firestore.\n     - Test timer countdown, progress bar color change when low, and automatic transition.\n     - Test tab-switch detection and violation alert deduction.\n     - Test result calculation, JSON file download, and base64 result code copy.\n     - Verify device lock and `#reset-quiz` hash behavior.\n3. **Constraint Auditing**:\n   - Grep for `//`, `/*`, and comments across all new source code to verify 100% compliance with Zero In-Code Documentation.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
