{"step_index":37,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:46:38Z","input_tokens":3485,"cache_read_tokens":51843,"output_tokens":468,"content":"**No, that is not correct** for this app.\n\nWith `if false;`, Cloud Firestore blocks **all** incoming reads and writes. That is why your site would receive `403 PERMISSION_DENIED`.\n\nTo allow the student quiz and teacher editor to fetch and save questions without requiring user login, change `false` to `true`:\n\n```javascript\nrules_version = '2';\n\nservice cloud.firestore {\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\n    match /{document=**} {\n      allow read, write: if true;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nAfter updating it to `true` and clicking **Publish** in the Firebase Console, both the student site and teacher editor will be able to read and write to Firestore.","thinking":"The provided rule explicitly denies all read and write access to Firestore. This explains the observed `403 PERMISSION_DENIED` errors. The rules effectively block all requests from the student and teacher sites, confirming the root cause of the access failures.\n\n\n"}
