ackground:var(--bg);color:var(--tx);border:2px solid var(--bd);margin-bottom:10px;font-weight:500;font-family:ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;font-size:.95rem;white-space:pre-wrap}\n26: .opt.sel{border-color:var(--pr);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pr) 14%,var(--bg))}\n27: .warn{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(0,0,0,.75);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:9;padding:20px}\n28: .warn .card{max-width:420px;text-align:center;border:2px solid var(--bad)}\n29: .big{font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--pr)}\n30: .fb{border-left:5px solid var(--bd)}\n31: .fb.ok{border-left-color:var(--ok)}.fb.no{border-left-color:var(--bad)}\n32: .tag{font-size:.8rem;font-weight:700;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:20px;color:#fff}\n33: .tag.ok{background:var(--ok)}.tag.no{background:var(--bad)}\n34: .fb pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:inherit;margin:8px 0;font-weight:600}\n35: .fb div{margin:4px 0;font-size:.95rem}\n36: .row{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n37: .nav{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(10,1fr);gap:6px;margin-top:16px}\n38: .nav button{padding:7px 0;font-size:.8rem;background:var(--bg);color:var(--mu);border:1px solid var(--bd)}\n39: .nav button.done{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--ok) 25%,var(--bg));color:var(--tx)}\n40: .nav button.cur{outline:2px solid var(--pr)}\n41: .ctl{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:6px}\n42: .ctl .sub{margin-left:auto;background:var(--ok)}\n43: </style>\n44: </head>\n45: <body>\n46: <div class=\"wrap\">\n47: \n48: <div id=\"start\" class=\"card\">\n49:   <h1>C Quiz: Switch Case</h1>\n50:   <p>20 items &bull; 20 seconds per question &bull; Do not switch tabs or windows.</p>\n51:   <label>Full Name<input id=\"nm\" placeholder=\"Juan Dela Cruz\" autocomplete=\"off\"></label>\n52:   <label>Section<input id=\"sc\" placeholder=\"e.g. BSIT 2-A\" autocomplete=\"off\"></label>\n53:   <ul>\n54:     <li>Each question has <b>20 seconds</b>. When time runs out, it moves on automatically with no points.</li>\n55:     <li>Every alt-tab or switch to another tab/app costs <b>-1 point</b>.</li>\n56:     <li>You cannot go back to previous questions.</li>\n57:     <li>Your score and per-question feedback appear right after the quiz.</li>\n58:   </ul>\n59:   <p id=\"err\" style=\"color:var(--bad);margin:0 0 10px\"></p>\n60:   <button id=\"go\">Start Quiz</button>\n61: </div>\n62: \n63: <div id=\"lock\" class=\"card hide\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n64:   <h1>You have already responded</h1>\n65:   <p id=\"lk1\">You can no longer open or retake this quiz.</p>\n66:   <p id=\"lk2\"></p>\n67:   <div class=\"row\" style=\"justify-content:center\"><button id=\"lkdl\" class=\"hide\">Download Result File</button></div>\n68: </div>\n69: \n70: <div id=\"exam\" class=\"hide\">\n71:   <div class=\"card\">\n72:     <div class=\"top\"><span id=\"prog\"></span><span id=\"sw\"></span><span id=\"tm\"></span></div>\n73:     <div class=\"bar\"><div id=\"tb\"></div></div>\n74:     <div id=\"q\"></div>\n75:     <div id=\"opts\"></div>\n76:     <button id=\"nx\">Next</button>\n77:   </div>\n78: </div>\n79: \n80: <div id=\"res\" class=\"hide\">\n81:   <div class=\"card\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n82:     <h1 id=\"rn\"></h1>\n83:     <div class=\"big\" id=\"rs\"></div>\n84:     <p id=\"rd\"></p>\n85:     <div class=\"row\" style=\"justify-content:center\">\n86:       <button id=\"dl\">Download Result File</button>\n87:       <button class=\"sec\" id=\"cp\">Copy Result Code</button>\n88:     </div>\n89:     <p style=\"font-size:.85rem\">Give the downloaded file or the result code to your instructor. Your result is also saved on this device.</p>\n90:   </div>\n91:   <h2>Feedback per Question</h2>\n92:   <div id=\"fbs\"></div>\n93: </div>\n94: </div>\n95: \n96: <div id=\"warn\" class=\"warn hide\"><div class=\"card\">\n97:   <h2 style=\"color:var(--bad)\">You left the quiz tab/window!</h2>\n98:   <p><b>-1 point</b> will be deducted from your score.<br>Total violations: <b id=\"wc\">0</b></p>\n99:   <button onclick=\"document.getElementById('warn').classList.add('hide')\">Continue</button>\n100: </div></div>\n101: \n102: <script>\n103: // Format: [question, [correct, wrong, wrong, wrong], explanation]  (choices are shuffled at runtime)\n104: const Q=[\n105: [\"Which C statement selects one of many code blocks to run based on the value of an expression?\",[\"switch\",\"for\",\"while\",\"goto\"],\"switch compares one expression against a list of constant case labels and runs the matching block.\"],\n106: [\"Which type of expression can be used as the controlling expression of a switch in C?\",[\"int or char\",\"float\",\"double\",\"string (char*)\"],\"switch works with integral types such as int and char, not floating-point values or strings.\"],\n107: [\"Which keyword prevents execution from falling through to the next case?\",[\"break\",\"continue\",\"return 0\",\"exit\"],\"break leaves the switch block immediately after the matching case finishes.\"],\n108: [\"When does the default label run?\",[\"When no case label matches\",\"Always, before the cases\",\"Only when the first case fails\",\"Only if break is missing\"],\"default is the fallback block used when no case matches the expression.\"],\n109: [\"What is the output?\\nint x = 2;\\nswitch (x) {\\n  case 1: printf(\\\"A\\\");\\n  case 2: printf(\\\"B\\\");\\n  case 3: printf(\\\"C\\\");\\n}\",[\"BC\",\"B\",\"C\",\"ABC\"],\"No break statements, so execution starts at case 2 and falls through to case 3.\"],\n110: [\"What is the output?\\nint x = 3;\\nswitch (x) {\\n  case 1: printf(\\\"1\\\"); break;\\n  default: printf(\\\"D\\\");\\n}\",[\"D\",\"1\",\"1D\",\"Nothing is printed\"],\"x is 3, no case matches, so default runs.\"],\n111: [\"Is the default label required in a switch statement?\",[\"No, it is optional\",\"Yes, always\",\"Yes, but only with char\",\"Only if there is no break\"],\"default is optional; without it, nothing runs when no case matches.\"],\n112: [\"Which case label is valid in C?\",[\"case 'A':\",\"case x:  (x is a variable)\",\"case 1.5:\",\"case \\\"A\\\":\"],\"Case labels must be integer or character constants. Variables, floats and strings are not allowed.\"],\n113: [\"What is the output?\\nchar c = 'b';\\nswitch (c) {\\n  case 'a': printf(\\\"1\\\"); break;\\n  case 'b': printf(\\\"2\\\");\\n  case 'c': printf(\\\"3\\\"); break;\\n}\",[\"23\",\"2\",\"3\",\"123\"],\"case 'b' matches and prints 2, has no break, then falls into case 'c' and prints 3 before break.\"],\n114: [\"What happens if two case labels in the same switch have the same constant value?\",[\"Compile-time error\",\"The first one runs\",\"The last one runs\",\"Both run\"],\"Duplicate case values are not allowed and the compiler reports an error.\"],\n115: [\"Where can the default label be placed inside a switch?\",[\"Anywhere inside the switch\",\"Only at the end\",\"Only at the beginning\",\"Only after a break\"],\"default may appear in any position; it is used only when no case matches.\"],\n116: [\"What is the output when x = 1?\\nswitch (x) {\\n  case 1:\\n  case 2: printf(\\\"Low\\\"); break;\\n  case 3: printf(\\\"High\\\");\\n}\",[\"Low\",\"High\",\"LowHigh\",\"Nothing is printed\"],\"Stacked labels share one block, so case 1 falls into case 2's code, which prints Low and breaks.\"],\n117: [\"Which is NOT allowed as the controlling expression of a switch in C?\",[\"A float variable, e.g. switch(f)\",\"An int variable, e.g. switch(x)\",\"A char variable, e.g. switch(c)\",\"An expression, e.g. switch(x % 3)\"],\"The controlling expression must be an integer type; float values are not allowed.\"],\n118: [\"Which statement about case labels is true?\",[\"They must be constant expressions\",\"They can be any variable\",\"They can be float values\",\"They can be strings\"],\"The compiler needs constant integer or character values to build the jump table.\"],\n119: [\"What is the output?\\nint x = 5;\\nswitch (x % 2) {\\n  case 0: printf(\\\"Even\\\"); break;\\n  case 1: printf(\\\"Odd\\\"); break;\\n}\",[\"Odd\",\"Even\",\"EvenOdd\",\"Nothing is printed\"],\"5 % 2 is 1, so case 1 runs.\"],\n120: [\"What is the output?\\nint x = 1;\\nswitch (x) {\\n  default: printf(\\\"D\\\");\\n  case 1: printf(\\\"1\\\"); break;\\n  case 2: printf(\\\"2\\\");\\n}\",[\"1\",\"D1\",\"D\",\"12\"],\"x matches case 1 directly, so default is skipped. Only 1 is printed, then break.\"],\n121: [\"When is switch preferred over an if-else if chain?\",[\"Comparing one variable against several constant values\",\"Testing ranges like x > 10\",\"Comparing strings\",\"Evaluating floating-point conditions\"],\"switch is designed for equality checks of one integral value against constants. It cannot test ranges.\"],\n122: [\"What is the value printed?\\nint a = 1;\\nswitch (a) {\\n  case 1: a++;\\n  case 2: a += 2; break;\\n  case 3: a = 10;\\n}\\nprintf(\\\"%d\\\", a);\",[\"4\",\"3\",\"2\",\"10\"],\"case 1 makes a = 2, falls into case 2 so a = 4, then break.\"],\n123: [\"Which is the correct switch syntax?\",[\"switch (x) { case 1: printf(\\\"One\\\"); break; }\",\"switch x { case 1: printf(\\\"One\\\"); break; }\",\"switch (x) { case 1 printf(\\\"One\\\"); break; }\",\"switch (x) { case(1) = printf(\\\"One\\\"); }\"],\"The expression goes in parentheses and each case label ends with a colon.\"],\n124: [\"Can a switch statement be nested inside another switch statement in C?\",[\"Yes\",\"No\",\"Only inside default\",\"Only with goto\"],\"Switch statements can be nested; each break only exits the innermost switch.\"]\n125: ];\n126: \n127: const PEN=1, SECS=20, LOCK='ds_quiz_switch_lock';\n128: const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);\n129: let timedOut=false,items=[],idx=0,sel=null,answers=[],switches=0,running=false,away=false,deadline=0,iv=null,startedAt=0,person={};\n130: \n131: function shuffle(a){for(let i=a.length-1;i>0;i--){const j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1));[a[i],a[j]]=[a[j],a[i]]}return a}\n132: \n133: $('go').onclick=()=>{\n134:   const n=$('nm').value.trim(),s=$('sc').value.trim();\n135:   if(!n||!s){$('err').textContent='Please enter your name and section first.';return}\n136:   try{if(localStorage.getItem(LOCK)){showLock();return}localStorage.setItem(LOCK,JSON.stringify({state:'started',n,s,ts:Date.now()}))}catch(e){}\n137:   person={n,s};\n138:   items=Q.map(([q,o,e])=>({q,e,opts:shuffle(o.map((t,k)=>({t,c:k===0})))}));\n139:   idx=0;answers=[];switches=0;running=true;startedAt=Date.now();\n140:   $('start').classList.add('hide');$('exam').classList.remove('hide');\n141:   show();\n142: };\n143: \n144: function show(){\n145:   const it=items[idx];sel=null;\n146:   $('prog').textContent='Question '+(idx+1)+' / '+items.length;\n147:   $('sw').textContent='Violations: '+switches;\n148:   $('q').textContent=(idx+1)+'. '+it.q;\n149:   const box=$('opts');box.innerHTML='';\n150:   it.opts.forEach((o,k)=>{\n151:     const b=document.createElement('button');b.className='opt';b.textContent=String.fromCharCode(65+k)+'. '+o.t;\n152:     b.onclick=()=>{sel=k;[...box.children].forEach((c,j)=>c.classList.toggle('sel',j===k))};\n153:     box.appendChild(b);\n154:   });\n155:   $('nx').textContent=idx===items.length-1?'Finish':'Next';\n156:   deadline=Date.now()+SECS*1000;\n157:   clearInterval(iv);iv=setInterval(tick,100);tick();\n158: }\n159: function tick(){\n160:   const left=Math.max(0,deadline-Date.now());\n161:   $('tm').textContent=Math.ceil(left/1000)+'s';\n162:   $('tb').style.width=(left/(SECS*1000)*100)+'%';\n163:   $('tb').classList.toggle('low',left<6000);\n164:   if(left<=0)next();\n165: }\n166: function next(){\n167:   clearInterval(iv);\n168:   answers[idx]=sel;\n169:   if(idx<items.length-1){idx++;show()}else finish();\n170: }\n171: $('nx').onclick=next;\n172: \n173: function violation(){\n174:   if(!running||away)return;\n175:   away=true;switches++;\n176:   $('sw').textContent='Violations: '+switches;\n177:   $('wc').textContent=switches;\n178:   $('warn').classList.remove('hide');\n179: }\n180: document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{document.hidden?violation():(away=false)});\n181: window.addEventListener('blur',violation);\n182: window.addEventListener('focus',()=>{away=false});\n183: \n184: function finish(){\n185:   if(!running)return;\n186:   running=false;clearInterval(iv);\n187:   let raw=0;items.forEach((it,i)=>{if(answers[i]!=null&&it.opts[answers[i]].c)raw++});\n188:   const pen=switches*PEN,final=Math.max(0,raw-pen);\n189:   const rec={n:person.n,s:person.s,raw,sw:switches,pen,sc:final,tot:items.length,ts:Date.now(),t:Math.round((Date.now()-startedAt)/1000)};\n190:   rec.code=btoa(unescape(encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(rec))));\n191:   try{const all=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ds_exam_results')||'[]');all.push(rec);localStorage.setItem('ds_exam_results',JSON.stringify(all))}catch(e){}\n192:   try{localStorage.setItem(LOCK,JSON.stringify({state:'done',rec}))}catch(e){}\n193:   $('exam').classList.add('hide');$('res').classList.remove('hide');\n194:   $('rn').textContent=person.n+' ('+person.s+')';\n195:   $('rs').textContent=final+' / '+items.length;\n196:   $('rd').textContent='Correct answers: '+raw+'  |  Tab-switch violations: '+switches+' (-'+pen+' pts)'+(timedOut?'':'');\n197:   const f=$('fbs');f.innerHTML='';\n198:   items.forEach((it,i)=>{\n199:     const a=answers[i],ok=a!=null&&it.opts[a].c;\n200:     const d=document.createElement('div');d.className='card fb '+(ok?'ok':'no');\n201:     const tag=document.createElement('span');tag.className='tag '+(ok?'ok':'no');tag.textContent=ok?'CORRECT':(a==null?'NO ANSWER':'WRONG');\n202:     const h=document.createElement('b');h.textContent='Question '+(i+1)+'  ';\n203:     const p=document.createElement('pre');p.textContent=it.q;\n204:     const y=document.createElement('div');y.textContent='Your answer: '+(a==null?'(no answer)':it.opts[a].t.replace(/\\n/g,' '));\n205:     const c=document.createElement('div');c.textContent='Correct answer: '+it.opts.find(o=>o.c).t.replace(/\\n/g,' ');\n206:     const e=document.createElement('div');e.style.color='var(--mu)';e.textContent='Explanation: '+it.e;\n207:     d.append(h,tag,p,y,c,e);f.appendChild(d);\n208:   });\n209:   $('dl').onclick=()=>{\n210:     const blob=new Blob([JSON.stringify(rec,null,2)],{type:'application/json'});\n211:     const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n212:     a.download='result_'+rec.n.replace(/\\W+/g,'_')+'_'+rec.s.replace(/\\W+/g,'_')+'.json';a.click();\n213:   };\n214:   $('cp').onclick=()=>{\n215:     const done=()=>{$('cp').textContent='Copied!'};\n216:     const manual=()=>{if(!$('codebox')){const t=document.createElement('textarea');t.id='codebox';t.readOnly=true;t.value=rec.code;t.style.cssText='width:100%;height:90px;margin-top:10px';$('cp').parentNode.after(t)}$('codebox').select()};\n217:     try{navigator.clipboard.writeText(rec.code).then(done).catch(manual)}catch(e){manual()}\n218:   };\n219:   window.scrollTo(0,0);\n220: }\n221: \n222: function dlRec(rec){\n223:   const blob=new Blob([JSON.stringify(rec,null,2)],{type:'application/json'});\n224:   const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n225:   a.download='result_'+rec.n.replace(/\\W+/g,'_')+'_'+rec.s.replace(/\\W+/g,'_')+'.json';a.click();\n226: }\n227: function showLock(){\n228:   let L=null;try{L=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(LOCK))}catch(e){}\n229:   $('start').classList.add('hide');$('exam').classList.add('hide');$('res').classList.add('hide');\n230:   $('lock').classList.remove('hide');\n231:   if(L&&L.state==='done'){\n232:     $('lk2').textContent='Your response has been recorded for '+L.rec.n+' ('+L.rec.s+'). Please wait for your instructor to announce the results.';\n233:     $('lkdl').classList.remove('hide');$('lkdl').onclick=()=>dlRec(L.rec);\n234:   }else if(L){\n235:     $('lk2').textContent='A quiz session for '+L.n+' ('+L.s+') was already started on this device and cannot be reopened. Please inform your instructor.';\n236:   }\n237: }\n238: function chkReset(){try{if(location.hash==='#reset-quiz'){localStorage.removeItem(LOCK);history.replaceState(null,'',location.pathname+location.search);location.reload()}}catch(e){}}\n239: window.addEventListener('hashchange',chkReset);chkReset();\n240: try{if(localStorage.getItem(LOCK))showLock()}catch(e){}\n241: </script>\n242: </body>\n243: </html>"}
{"step_index":6,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:47:40Z","input_tokens":6545,"cache_read_tokens":26457,"output_tokens":1362,"thinking":"Initial assessment: The user requires a web application hosted on a platform, utilizing a database to manage quizzes. There are two distinct components: a quiz-taking interface that pulls questions and distractors and a separate teacher interface for question creation and management. The teacher interface must support auto-numbering, question/answer input, and answer marking.\n\n\nThe teacher interface design needs a clear UI with auto-numbering, question/answer input, and answer-marking features. Functionality includes adding new questions with a \"+\" button, randomization of questions and answers, and an option button for UI rendering. Firebase configuration for the application is available. Patching strategy is dependent on whether or not the patch is deemed a major change.\n\n\nInvestigation reveals strict constraints on code modifications. UI changes are permitted, but no APK building or modifications to original files are allowed. Any updates require explicit permission and a detailed verification plan covering affected files, dependencies, and critical flows, documented in the implementation plan. Mandatory investigation and research are required before implementing any code change.\n\n\nInvestigation focuses on codebase optimization. The goal is to identify and implement the most efficient algorithms, reduce time complexity, and eliminate redundancies while preserving correctness and maintainability. A strict workflow mandating investigation, research, analysis, and an implementation plan, followed by explicit approval before any code modification, will be enforced.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"Test-Path HISTORY.md","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Check if HISTORY.md exists"}}]}
