{"step_index":9,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:47:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T04:47:57+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T04:48:00+08:00\nThe search for \"firebase 10 firestore modular cdn gstatic unpkg\" returned the following summary:\nTo use the **Firebase 10+ Modular Web SDK** directly via a CDN (without using a build tool like Webpack, Vite, or npm), you should use **Google's official `gstatic` CDN** with native browser ES modules (`type=\"module\"`). \n\nWhile networks like **UNPKG** or **jsDelivr** host Firebase packages[1], Firebase officially recommends and hosts the bundled browser-ready modular ES modules directly on `gstatic`[2].\n\n### 1. Using Google's Official `gstatic` CDN (Recommended for Vanilla JS)\n\nHere is how to set up Firebase 10 Firestore using native ES module imports in your HTML file:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <title>Firebase 10 Firestore CDN Example</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n    <h1>My Firebase 10 App</h1>\n\n    <script type=\"module\">\n        // Import the functions you need from the SDKs on the gstatic CDN\n        import { initializeApp } from \"https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-app.js\";\n        import { getFirestore, collection, addDoc, getDocs } from \"https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-firestore.js\";\n\n        // Your web app's Firebase configuration\n        const firebaseConfig = {\n            apiKey: \"YOUR_API_KEY\",\n            authDomain: \"YOUR_PROJECT_ID.firebaseapp.com\",\n            projectId: \"YOUR_PROJECT_ID\",\n            storageBucket: \"YOUR_PROJECT_ID.appspot.com\",\n            messagingSenderId: \"YOUR_SENDER_ID\",\n            appId: \"YOUR_APP_ID\"\n        };\n\n        // Initialize Firebase\n        const app = initializeApp(firebaseConfig);\n\n        // Initialize Cloud Firestore and get a reference to the service\n        const db = getFirestore(app);\n\n        // Example: Writing data to Firestore\n        async function writeData() {\n            try {\n                const docRef = await addDoc(collection(db, \"users\"), {\n                    first: \"Ada\",\n                    last: \"Lovelace\",\n                    born: 1815\n                });\n                console.log(\"Document written with ID: \", docRef.id);\n            } catch (e) {\n                console.error(\"Error adding document: \", e);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Example: Reading data from Firestore\n        async function readData() {\n            const querySnapshot = await getDocs(collection(db, \"users\"));\n            querySnapshot.forEach((doc) => {\n                console.log(`${doc.id} =>`, doc.data());\n            });\n        }\n\n        writeData();\n        readData();\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Using UNPKG or jsDelivr (Alternative CDN)\n\nIf your environment specifically requires **UNPKG** or **jsDelivr**, you must target the specific modular npm packages (`@firebase/app` and `@firebase/firestore`). Because these npm packages rely on internal dependencies, pointing straight to them via browser ESM requires proper path resolution. \n\nUsing **esm.sh** or **jsDelivr** with `esm` support handles these dependencies automatically:\n\n```html\n<script type=\"module\">\n    // Using jsDelivr's ESM endpoint which automatically resolves internal package dependencies\n    import { initializeApp } from \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/firebase@10.14.0/+esm\";\n    import { getFirestore, collection, getDocs } from \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@firebase/firestore@10.14.0/+esm\";\n\n    // Configuration and initialization logic goes here...\n</script>\n```\n\n### Key Rules to Remember:\n1. **`type=\"module\"` is mandatory:** Browser ES module imports (`import ... from \"...\"`) only work inside script tags explicitly marked with `type=\"module\"`[3].\n2. **Version matching:** Always ensure that all Firebase service imports (`firebase-app.js`, `firebase-firestore.js`, etc.) share the **exact same version number** (e.g., `10.14.0`) to avoid mismatched internal dependency errors.\n\nSources:\n[1] [jsdelivr.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEHgSL24OfMJjGW8a-QPI9fGFO1QwT1M-a1Wua8Pp0veWC2bUsX3HZ_ekTiWlTA7S-HbO5KWjr98kTzEq_rvjWU3Wa5B4Jk_rzPdmxwRp2PIElFrFy3yDeBrH_I7jAxaEI5Tg==)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHLmRtlPNxWH1J3jqRyLAd7kl7NSy7qp7JeZqs-sziyCj3wg3yihvY2L4eKVvYomQM9TxRLhNGacF1NjK1vC4QEEsqPlRv4vP30UC94UvRCB9nRxxHa3qOMW_uPb5T7tw==)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHS1IvUEFSQiHcMdXfMmtcLR7AnmPvjKA3b8fgeqbXgCx5PjxbVumrx76z-1cFhyqkSUG8FQ8lnYg7BshvHIoc_yhR8ghck3q9PHEfTCPcu9rxKMizRQFeUsFlPqRB3JGjmi_rNQd8qWCZpwt5p7pPQ-yPBRMc2cyqS0HuP162DOeA5NVJl-Gl9PbUT_V0pleJ-I2m8d5rfAI_AS8izrSfP)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
