{"step_index":32,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:49:06Z","input_tokens":2239,"cache_read_tokens":38326,"output_tokens":6954,"thinking":"Firestore successfully confirms basic connectivity and permission verification. The API key and Firebase credentials are validated as operational. The next step involves a detailed examination of the user's project to draw questions and render them on a Vercel site using Firebase.\n\n\nThe initial focus is on structuring the quiz application based on the provided HTML template, specifically `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`. This involves rendering questions and answers, including UI elements like progress bars, timers, and randomized options. The design will be strictly derived from the given HTML.\n\n\nStructuring the quiz application involves several UI elements derived from the HTML template. Key features include end screens displaying results (score, correct answers, violations, download and copy result), feedback for each question, a lock screen for device restrictions, and integration with Firebase for saving student submissions. Additional considerations are timers, question/answer randomization, and tab-switching violation penalties, all configurable through quiz settings. A teacher portal will be developed using the exact same design language and CSS classes.\n\n\nDeveloping the teacher portal necessitates UI elements mirroring the student quiz interface for a consistent user experience. This includes buttons and toggles for settings like answer randomization, tab-switching penalties, and timer durations. A key component is a dynamically numbered question list, facilitating question creation, modification, and deletion along with Firebase integration for saving and loading quizzes.\n\nInitial project configuration on Vercel suggests using a simple `index.html` file to deploy the student quiz.\n\n\nInitial deployment strategy looks straightforward: deploy both `index.html` (student quiz) and `teacher.html` (teacher portal) to the root directory on Vercel. Both HTML files are instantly deployable as static content, no build step required.\n\nConsidering the user's rules: The focus is now on adherence to rule-based constraints around updates, particularly those concerning patch management in `HISTORY.md` and verification planning within `implementation_plan.md`. The instruction explicitly prohibits modification of original codebase apart from UI elements and mandates comprehensive verification of all changes.\n\n\nThe rules emphasize adherence to a strict workflow that prioritizes investigation, research, and approval before implementation, especially regarding UI element updates. Research is essential before implementing any requested code change, focusing on efficient algorithms, minimizing resource usage, and eliminating redundant logic, all while preserving correctness and maintainability. Every code change must follow a defined sequence: investigation, research, analysis, plan preparation, approval, implementation, and verification, with explicit approval needed before each implementation.\n\n\nThe rules emphasize stringent codebase constraints, including no in-code documentation, strict adherence to the approved plan, and comprehensive verification of all changes. Zero improvisation is permitted; any necessary additions require prior explanation and approval. Verification must include checks on modified files, related elements, and critical flows, documented with results and limitations, and success requires documented evidence. Modification is limited to UI elements only.\n\n\nThe HTML file should not be modified, only used to derive the UI elements; the prohibition includes its deletion or alteration. Generated code must have no in-code documentation or comments of any kind. Firebase Firestore is the data store, with a specific document schema for quiz data. The document schema outlines a structure for quizzes, including title, description, and settings such as time limits.\n\n\nThe quiz data structure requires parsing the provided JSON, extracting and applying settings, and using randomization via the Fisher-Yates algorithm for questions and answers. Event delegation optimizes responsiveness. A single interval timer with delta calculation manages time precisely, and handling for tab visibility changes ensures accurate penalty application, with the whole application immediately deployable to Vercel without a build step.\n\n\nPreserving the data serialization format (`btoa(unescape(encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(rec))))`) ensures backward compatibility with existing grading scripts. Strict adherence to the provided HTML's styling is paramount, including CSS variable definitions and all UI elements.  The student quiz (`index.html`) requires screens for start, exam, results, and lock states, while the teacher editor (`teacher.html`) mirrors the visual theme with added top controls and options.\n\n\nThe teacher portal design necessitates a numbered question list with interactive elements for question creation and modification as detailed, including input fields for prompts, answers, and explanations, along with a delete button and an append button for new questions. UI control elements for settings like answer and question randomization, tab-switching violations, and timer configuration will also be incorporated, as requested. The UI will strictly adhere to the provided HTML template.\n\n\nRule analysis begins. `HISTORY.md` doesn't exist yet, so the initial release will be considered a major patch, tentatively version 1.0.0, or Patch 1. A `HISTORY.md` plan will be prepared. Rules 5 and 6 concerning the implementation plan and approval workflow are noted. The mandatory execution workflow (Rule 8) dictates investigation, research, analysis, planning, approval, implementation, and verification before any code changes.\n\n\nThe next step is creating the `implementation_plan.md` artifact, specifying the proposed project architecture and file structure. This plan includes `firebase-config.js` for Firebase interaction, `index.html` for the student quiz, `teacher.html` for the teacher portal, `vercel.json` for Vercel configuration, and an initial `HISTORY.md` entry. The plan must be completed before any code modification. Before proceeding, explicit approval is required.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan for Firebase-backed Student and Teacher Quiz Web Application ready for Vercel deployment, strictly adhering to the original design, zero in-code comments, and mandatory verification procedures.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan: Firebase-Backed Student & Teacher Quiz Web Application\n\n## 1. Overview & Requirements\nTransform the standalone quiz into a two-part web application deployable directly to Vercel, integrated with Cloud Firestore using the provided Firebase credentials:\n1. **Student Quiz (`index.html`)**: Fetches active questions, distractors, and configuration directly from Firestore. Faithfully preserves the visual design, typography, color tokens, and layout from `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`. Implements the timer, auto-randomization of questions and choices, anti-cheating tab-switch detection and scoring penalties, detailed post-quiz feedback, JSON download, and base64 result code export.\n2. **Teacher Editor (`teacher.html`)**: Built using the exact same design language and CSS tokens. Features auto-numbered question cards where the teacher can tap and type the question, correct answer box, and three distractor (wrong answer) boxes. Provides a `+` button to append new questions, and an **Options** button rendering a settings modal/UI for toggling auto-randomize questions, auto-randomize answers, tab-switch violation penalty, and timer duration. Allows saving directly to Firestore and loading pre-existing or default quiz sets.\n3. **Vercel Deployment Configuration (`vercel.json`)**: Configures static routing and clean URLs for zero-build deployment.\n4. **Changelog Tracking (`HISTORY.md`)**: Establishes Patch 1.0.0 (Major release) under user Rule 1.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Proposed Architecture & Files\n\n### Files to Create / Modify\n- [firebase-config.js](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/firebase-config.js): Shared Firebase 10 Modular Web SDK integration via Google's official `gstatic` CDN. Exports initialized Firebase app, Firestore instance, and data access methods (`getQuiz`, `saveQuiz`, `saveSubmission`).\n- [index.html](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html): Student Quiz client. Identical CSS styling and visual components derived from `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`.\n- [teacher.html](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html): Teacher Quiz Authoring Portal. Uses matching CSS design system, auto-numbered question inputs, options modal, and Firestore synchronization.\n- [vercel.json](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/vercel.json): Vercel configuration for static routing and caching headers.\n- [HISTORY.md](file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md): Patch history tracking starting with Patch 1.0.0.\n- `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`: Kept untouched as the original reference file per Rule 2 & Rule 12.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Component Specifications\n\n### 3.1 Student Quiz (`index.html`)\n- **Theme & Tokens**: Exact `:root` CSS variables (`--bg`, `--card`, `--tx`, `--mu`, `--pr`, `--ok`, `--bad`, `--bd`) and dark mode media query from `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`.\n- **Start Screen**: Student Full Name and Section inputs; quiz metadata display; \"Start Quiz\" button; local storage check to prevent re-taking already locked responses.\n- **Exam Engine**:\n  - Live timer bar (`#tb`) and countdown text (`#tm`).\n  - Active question prompt (`#q`) and monospace answer choice buttons (`.opt`) with `A.`, `B.`, `C.`, `D.` prefixes.\n  - Anti-cheat tracking: `visibilitychange` and window `blur` event listeners with debouncing to prevent duplicate penalties.\n  - Warning modal (`#warn`) showing current violation count and deducted points.\n- **Results & Feedback Screen**:\n  - Score tally (`#rs`), participant badge, correct answers count, and violation deductions.\n  - Base64 result encoding (`btoa(unescape(encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(rec))))`) matching original format.\n  - Download Result File (`.json`) button and Copy Result Code button.\n  - Question-by-question breakdown with `.fb.ok` (green) and `.fb.no` (red) cards showing student response, correct answer, and explanation.\n\n### 3.2 Teacher Portal (`teacher.html`)\n- **Visual Design**: Strict visual continuity using the exact card, input, and button styles.\n- **Top Bar & Actions**:\n  - Quiz Title & Description inputs.\n  - \"Options\" Button: Opens a modal/panel containing:\n    - Auto-randomize questions toggle.\n    - Auto-randomize answers toggle.\n    - Switching tab violation toggle & penalty points input.\n    - Timer toggle & seconds-per-question input.\n  - \"Save to Firebase\" button: Pushes the active quiz definition to Firestore collection `quizzes`, document `active`.\n  - \"Load Default C Quiz\" button: Pre-populates all 20 switch-case questions from the original quiz file for instant editing and testing.\n  - \"Open Student Quiz\" link/button.\n- **Auto-Numbered Questions Container**:\n  - Dynamic list with questions numbered sequentially (`Question 1`, `Question 2`, ...).\n  - Tappable/typeable question prompt (`textarea`/`input`).\n  - Tappable/typeable **Correct Answer** box (highlighted with `--ok` green border).\n  - Tappable/typeable **Wrong Answer 1** box.\n  - Tappable/typeable **Wrong Answer 2** box.\n  - Tappable/typeable **Wrong Answer 3** box.\n  - Optional explanation box.\n  - Delete question button (with instant re-numbering of subsequent items).\n- **Add Question (`+`) Button**:\n  - Prominently placed at the bottom to append a new blank question card and increment the question counter.\n\n### 3.3 Firebase & Cloud Firestore Integration\n- **SDK Import**: Modular ES modules loaded via `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-app.js` and `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-firestore.js`.\n- **Data Model**:\n  - Document path: `quizzes/active`\n  - Fields:\n    - `title`: string\n    - `description`: string\n    - `settings`: `{ timePerQuestion: number, enableTimer: boolean, enableTabViolation: boolean, tabViolationPenalty: number, randomizeQuestions: boolean, randomizeAnswers: boolean }`\n    - `questions`: Array of `{ q: string, correct: string, wrongs: string[], explanation: string }`\n    - `updatedAt`: timestamp\n- **Fallback Capability**: If Firestore is initially empty or offline, fallback to the pre-packaged default C switch-case quiz questions so the app is always functional.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Optimization & Architectural Rationale (Rule 7)\n- **Time Complexity**: Fisher-Yates shuffle runs in optimal $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ time and $\\mathcal{O}(1)$ space for both questions and choices.\n- **DOM & Memory**: Event delegation on the answer options box and question container minimizes event listeners and garbage collection churn.\n- **Zero Build / CDN**: Zero bundling step required; natively compatible with modern browsers and instant deployment on Vercel static hosting.\n- **Zero In-Code Comments (Rule 9)**: No comments, docstrings, or TODOs will be written into any source code files.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Potential Risks & Mitigations\n- **Risk**: Student network latency or Firestore read failure.\n  - **Mitigation**: Implement graceful offline fallback to local cached quiz data or default questions if Firestore fetch fails or returns empty.\n- **Risk**: Simultaneous `blur` and `visibilitychange` events triggering double penalties.\n  - **Mitigation**: State lock flag (`away`) prevents multiple increment calls during a single tab-switch cycle until focus is restored.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Verification Plan Across Affected Files & Devices (Rule 3 & Rule 10)\n\n### 6.1 Files Under Verification\n- `firebase-config.js`\n- `index.html`\n- `teacher.html`\n- `vercel.json`\n- `HISTORY.md`\n\n### 6.2 Verification Steps & Test Cases\n1. **Teacher Authoring Flow**:\n   - Open `teacher.html` in browser.\n   - Click \"Load Default C Quiz\": Verify all 20 questions populate with correct answer and 3 wrong answers.\n   - Click `+` button: Verify Question 21 appends with proper auto-numbering.\n   - Click \"Options\": Toggle randomize questions, randomize answers, adjust timer to 15s, toggle tab violation penalty. Save options.\n   - Click \"Save to Firebase\": Verify status changes to \"Saved successfully\" and verify Firestore document `quizzes/active` is written.\n2. **Student Quiz Flow**:\n   - Open `index.html` in browser.\n   - Verify quiz title, description, and settings load directly from Firestore.\n   - Enter Full Name and Section, click \"Start Quiz\".\n   - Verify auto-randomized questions and choices appear with A-D labels.\n   - Verify timer countdown operates accurately at 100ms intervals.\n   - Tab Switch Test: Switch to another window/tab, then switch back. Verify `#warn` overlay appears, violation count increments to 1, and points deduct accordingly.\n   - Complete Quiz: Answer questions and click Finish.\n   - Result Verification: Verify final score accounts for tab violation penalty. Verify base64 code can be copied to clipboard and JSON result file downloads correctly with student name and section.\n   - Lockout Test: Reload page and verify the student cannot re-take the quiz without resetting.\n3. **Cross-Device & Responsive Verification**:\n   - Test responsive layout on mobile viewport (<480px), tablet (768px), and desktop.\n   - Test dark mode (`prefers-color-scheme: dark`) rendering.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
